WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.810
Delhi, 1675.

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:09.010
The ninth Sikh Guru, Tegh Bahadur, is executed
on the orders of the emperor Aurangzeb.

3
00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:13.210
Today a gurdwara in Delhi,
Sis Ganj, marks the place,

4
00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.820
and Sikhs honour him as a martyr.

5
00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:19.090
Yet Sikh tradition also
speaks of dharam yudh:

6
00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:21.600
a war fought for righteousness.

7
00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.300
So when can a war be righteous?

8
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.470
And why honour those who
refused to fight back?

9
00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.330
In this mission, you'll build
the gate a war must pass through,

10
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.050
one lock at a time.

11
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.680
Then you'll weigh up whether dharam yudh
can still justify Sikhs using force today.

12
00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:42.750
Your mission: find out when Sikhs
think a war can be righteous,

13
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.790
and why they honour martyrs
who did not fight back.
